WEBVTT

00:00:01.062 --> 00:00:06.662
Welcome to vNAAATS. In this video, you will learn how to use the flight data display or FDD.

00:00:06.982 --> 00:00:13.798
tracking, releasing and transferring aircraft, changing a flight level, speed or SELCAL, and handing over to a relief controller.

00:00:15.686 --> 00:00:21.414
Please note this is a demonstration using sample flights. It is not a live version of the FDD.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.110
Open the FDD and enter your key.

00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:39.078
The display waits until you are connected to VATSIM on an oceanic position, then opens on that position by itself. To work in natTrak, use the Open natTrak link and sign in there with your VATSIM details.

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:43.718
The main list shows the flights heading for oceanic airspace, grouped by track.

00:00:44.582 --> 00:00:49.222
natTrak requests waiting for action are on the left, and cleared flights are on the right.

00:00:49.574 --> 00:00:55.366
The show menu limits the list of flights close to entering or leaving, and you can group and sort it however suits you.

00:00:56.102 --> 00:00:58.502
Click a call sign to open the aircraft menu.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:02.246
In the history lists, a click on a call sign opens its flight plan.

00:01:02.566 --> 00:01:06.342
The flight plan and the NATTRAC data for that aircraft appear on the right.

00:01:07.046 --> 00:01:10.182
To take an aircraft, choose Track, then press Track Aircraft.

00:01:10.502 --> 00:01:13.158
The plugin types the command into EuroScope for you.

00:01:13.894 --> 00:01:15.846
to change a flight level or speed.

00:01:16.294 --> 00:01:20.518
Select the new flight level or Mach number in the same menu and press Update Aircraft.

00:01:20.966 --> 00:01:23.814
The change is sent to EuroScope and saved for everyone.

00:01:24.582 --> 00:01:28.454
For SELCAL, open the SELCAL tab, type the four-letter code and press send.

00:01:28.806 --> 00:01:32.006
You can also copy the command or save the code against the flight.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.262
When the aircraft leaves you, open the menu and choose release tag.

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:42.374
Pass it to another controller, choose transfer, pick the controller who is online and press transfer.

00:01:42.726 --> 00:01:46.470
When an aircraft nears its boundary, the handoff button flashes to remind you.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.358
There is a separate video on that.

00:01:49.126 --> 00:01:52.422
If a pilot is not talking to you, choose contact me and press send.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:57.446
Plug in clicks the call sign on the tag for you and the display tells you if it did not land.

00:01:57.798 --> 00:02:01.862
The flight is marked and turns red if there is still no track after 20 minutes.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:07.526
If you need a supervisor, choose the red supervisor button, write your message and copy the wallop.

00:02:10.886 --> 00:02:15.910
To hand your whole position to a relief controller, open the position menu and choose relief.

00:02:16.198 --> 00:02:19.110
Pick the controller who is taking over and start the handover.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.862
your aircraft are passed across automatically.

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:28.742
If you work on more than one screen, the CPDLC window and the TrackAudio history each have a pop out button.

00:02:29.158 --> 00:02:32.678
It opens them in a window of their own that you can drag to another screen.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.350
That is the flight data display.

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:42.406
In the next videos we cover CPDLC and using natTrak through the FDD.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.778
Thanks for watching.

